<!-- ══ SLIDE 7 — Q3a: CHALLENGES ══ -->
<div class="slide bg-b">
  <div class="shead"><div class="label">Q3a · Challenges Going Forward</div><div class="snum">07 / 10</div></div>
  <h2 class="stitle">What <em>Challenges</em> Does P&amp;G Face?</h2>
  <div class="cgrid">
    <div class="citem">
      <span class="cico">🔄</span>
      <div class="ctitle">Change Management &amp; Data Culture</div>
      <p>"We had to educate and train our field force over and over again to make analytics part of their daily routine" <span class="cite">(IBS, 'Challenges')</span></p>
    </div>
    <div class="citem">
      <span class="cico">🏢</span>
      <div class="ctitle">Fragmented Data Ownership</div>
      <p>"Ownership of data is fragmented across IT, engineering, finance and procurement" — Siemens USA CEO E. Spiegel <span class="cite">(IBS, 'Challenges')</span></p>
    </div>
    <div class="citem">
      <span class="cico">🔐</span>
      <div class="ctitle">System Reliability &amp; Security</div>
      <p>"If we have a security issue on one of our websites, that could impact the company's reputation instantaneously" — Passerini <span class="cite">(IBS, 'Challenges')</span></p>
    </div>
    <div class="citem">
      <span class="cico">🛡️</span>
      <div class="ctitle">Consumer Privacy — GDPR</div>
      <p>Consumer profiling (Pampers.com, Consumer Pulse) triggers GDPR obligations on profiling and automated decisions with potential "intrusive effects on individuals" <span class="cite">(GDPR Art. 4.4 &amp; 22)</span></p>
    </div>
    <div class="citem">
      <span class="cico">🤖</span>
      <div class="ctitle">EU AI Act Compliance</div>
      <p>HR analytics, marketing AI, and consumer prediction may qualify as <strong>high-risk AI</strong>, requiring strict documentation and oversight <span class="cite">(EU AI Act 2024/1689)</span></p>
    </div>
    <div class="citem">
      <span class="cico">📉</span>
      <div class="ctitle">Big Data ≠ Strategy</div>
      <p>P&amp;G lost market share for 14 of 17 quarters despite world-class analytics. Analytics must serve the business strategy, not substitute it <span class="cite">(IBS, 'Challenges')</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="spk">Teresa Miranda</div>
</div>

<!-- ══ SLIDE 8 — Q3b: RECOMMENDATIONS ══ -->
<div class="slide bg-a">
  <div class="shead"><div class="label">Q3b · Recommendations</div><div class="snum">08 / 10</div></div>
  <h2 class="stitle">What Should P&amp;G <em>Do?</em></h2>
  <div class="rlist">
    <div class="ritem">
      <div class="rnum">1</div>
      <div>
        <div class="rtitle">Formalise a Data Governance Framework — DAMA DMBOK2</div>
        <p>Appoint CDO with business sponsorship. Define Data Owners &amp; Data Stewards per domain. Business Glossary, metadata catalogue, data quality policies. P&amp;G already appointed Guy Peri as CDO in 2015 — next step: institutionalise governance beyond a single role <span class="cite">(IBS, 'Big Data at P&amp;G')</span></p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="ritem">
      <div class="rnum">2</div>
      <div>
        <div class="rtitle">Conduct a BDA Maturity Assessment — Info-Tech Model</div>
        <p>Based on case evidence (Hadoop, CDO, analytics in all functions), P&amp;G qualifies as <strong>Innovator — Level 4</strong>: "big data treated as an asset used to innovate with new products and services." Formal assessment identifies remaining gaps and defines a roadmap</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="ritem">
      <div class="rnum">3</div>
      <div>
        <div class="rtitle">Embed GDPR — Privacy by Design (Art. 25, 30, 35)</div>
        <p>Record of Processing Activities (Art. 30); DPIAs before high-risk consumer analytics (Art. 35); data minimisation — collect only what is strictly necessary; consumer rights (access, rectification, erasure) operationally supported</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="ritem">
      <div class="rnum">4</div>
      <div>
        <div class="rtitle">Prepare for EU AI Act — Regulation EU 2024/1689</div>
        <p>Document all AI systems; implement transparency and human oversight for HR analytics and marketing AI; align with the risk-based framework (unacceptable / high / limited / minimal risk)</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="ritem">
      <div class="rnum">5</div>
      <div>
        <div class="rtitle">Balance Analytics with the Human Touch</div>
        <p>Complement quantitative models with qualitative consumer research — especially in beauty and baby care, where emotional connection drives brand loyalty. "Big Data gives no guidance on how to ask the right questions"</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="spk">Teresa Miranda</div>
</div>

